# waifu2x-ncnn-vulkan Binary

This folder should contain the waifu2x-ncnn-vulkan executable and models.

## Download

Get the latest release for your platform:
<https://github.com/nihui/waifu2x-ncnn-vulkan/releases>

- **Windows:** `waifu2x-ncnn-vulkan-YYYYMMDD-windows.zip`
- **Linux:** `waifu2x-ncnn-vulkan-YYYYMMDD-ubuntu.zip`
- **macOS:** `waifu2x-ncnn-vulkan-YYYYMMDD-macos.zip`

## Installation

Extract the downloaded archive into this folder. The structure should look like:

```
tools/
  waifu2x-ncnn-vulkan/
    waifu2x-ncnn-vulkan.exe   (or waifu2x-ncnn-vulkan on Linux/Mac)
    models-cunet/
    models-upconv_7_anime_style_art_rgb/
    models-upconv_7_photo/
    vcomp140.dll              (Windows only)
    LICENSE
    README.md
```

## Alternative: System PATH

Instead of placing the files here, you can:

1. Extract the binary anywhere on your system
2. Add that folder to your system PATH environment variable
3. The svg-optimizer tool will automatically find it

## Usage

Once installed, waifu2x will be automatically detected and available as an upscaling option:

```bash
svg-optimizer image.png --upscale --upscale-method waifu2x
```

## Notes

- The binary files are excluded from git (see .gitignore)
- waifu2x is optional. Real-ESRGAN and Lanczos upscalers work without it
- waifu2x specializes in line art with configurable noise reduction
